# reda baked netlist -- generated, do not edit by hand.
# Regenerate with: cargo run --release --bin bake_verilog
#
# The gate-level netlist Yosys produced for the source named below, read
# back by `reda::frontend`. It is checked in so a build that cannot run
# Yosys -- the browser viewer's wasm32 build above all -- can still load a
# synthesised circuit. A stale copy would misrepresent this project's own
# compiler, so `the_baked_netlists_match_fresh_synthesis` re-synthesizes
# and fails unless a fresh run renders byte-for-byte identically to this
# file.
#
# A gate's kind is `topology::GateKind::wire_name`. Two of them are what
# redstone builds directly: `gate nor y <- a b` is NOR(a, b) driving `y`,
# and `gate merge y <- a b` is a wire merge -- no torch and no gate body at
# all, just the point where `a`'s and `b`'s dust are allowed to touch.
# Every other kind (`and`, `nand`, `xor`, `mux`, ...) is gate level, and
# `compile::lowering` expands it into those two.
#
# 31 gates, 4 inputs, 7 outputs.
# cells: nor2:3 merge2:6 and:5 nand:9 andnot:6 ornot:1 mux:1
circuit verilog:seven_segment
source tests/fixtures/seven_segment.v
